        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jacques-Yves Cousteau, Louis Malle\n- Works: The Silent World, Zeitgeist, And the Pursuit of Happiness\n- Events: 1956 Cannes Film Festival\n- Topics: documentary films, conspiracy theories, immigrants in the United States\n\nFacts:\n- The Silent World is a 1956 French documentary film co-directed by Jacques-Yves Cousteau and Louis Malle.\n- At the 1956 Cannes Film Festival, the Palme d'Or went to The Silent World by Jacques-Yves Cousteau and Louis Malle.\n- And the Pursuit of Happiness is a 1986 documentary film directed by Louis Malle about the experiences of immigrants in the United States during the 1980s.\n- Zeitgeist is a series of three documentary films released between 2007 and 2011 that present conspiracy theories and proposals for broad social and economic changes.",
